/P 124 0 R
/T (The distribution of RFM scores shows two dominant peaks, corresponding to the extreme groups \(111 and 555\). In the middle range, customer segments are more heterogeneous, with relatively similar frequencies across most combinations. However, there is a slight shift towards higher-value profiles, and some combinations are not present or only appear rarely. This pattern suggests that customer behaviour is concentrated in a few recurring groups, such as sporadic, low-engaged buyers or high-value segments.)
/E (The distribution of RFM scores shows two dominant peaks, corresponding to the extreme groups \(111 and 555\). In the middle range, customer segments are more heterogeneous, with relatively similar frequencies across most combinations. However, there is a slight shift towards higher-value profiles, and some combinations are not present or only appear rarely. This pattern suggests that customer behaviour is concentrated in a few recurring groups, such as sporadic, low-engaged buyers or high-value segments.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
