/T (The frequency-recency matrix suggests that customers characterized by both high purchase frequency and recent transactions have the greatest expected number of future purchases. Instead, the expected transaction rate decreases for customers whose last purchase occurred further in the past, even if their purchase frequency is relatively high. In addition, customers with fewer transactions but recent purchasing activity may have a high probability of also making future purchases.)
/E (The frequency-recency matrix suggests that customers characterized by both high purchase frequency and recent transactions have the greatest expected number of future purchases. Instead, the expected transaction rate decreases for customers whose last purchase occurred further in the past, even if their purchase frequency is relatively high. In addition, customers with fewer transactions but recent purchasing activity may have a high probability of also making future purchases.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
269 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 127 0 R
/T (The probability alive matrix indicates that customers with both high purchase frequency and recent transactions have the strongest probability of being active. In contrast, this probability decreases as the time since the last purchase increases, even among customers with a significant number of past orders. Therefore, recency emerges as a significant predictor of customer activity, as individuals with fewer purchases may still have a high probability of being active if they have purchased recently.  )
/E (The probability alive matrix indicates that customers with both high purchase frequency and recent transactions have the strongest probability of being active. In contrast, this probability decreases as the time since the last purchase increases, even among customers with a significant number of past orders. Therefore, recency emerges as a significant predictor of customer activity, as individuals with fewer purchases may still have a high probability of being active if they have purchased recently.  )
/Pg 27 0 R
