>>
endobj
276 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 129 0 R
/E (The main findings obtained through RFM analysis and CLV modelling represent an essential guidance tool for shaping marketing strategies and supporting managerial decision-making. First, the ability to segment customers into Bronze, Silver, Gold, and Platinum levels based on their predicted Customer Lifetime Value for the next six months allows the business to develop effective tiered loyalty programs. In particular, exclusive benefits, personalized incentives, and tailored communication campaigns should target the small share of high-value customers that contribute significantly to overall revenue. Focusing on these customers can help improve retention rates, strengthen long-term relationships, and maximize future profitability. At the same time, the identification of customers who are at risk of churning, mainly because they have not purchased recently, provides an opportunity to implement targeted win-back campaigns. Although these individuals currently generate only a limited share of revenue, personalized discounts or promotional offers may encourage them to return and make further purchases.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
277 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 129 0 R
/E (In addition, customer segmentation based on recency, frequency, and monetary value allows the company to develop communication and promotional strategies tailored to the characteristics of each group. Therefore, customers can receive more relevant messages, product recommendations, and offers, increasing both engagement and loyalty. For example, high-value customers may benefit from exclusive rewards and personalized offers, while customers at risk of churning may be interested in discounts and short-term promotions. This personalized approach can improve customer satisfaction and strengthen relationships over time. Furthermore, the analysis of top product categories within each customer segment highlights Beverages as the main preference shared by the majority of customers. Although this category is not the largest source of overall revenue, it generates a high number of recurring purchases and helps maintain a high level of customer engagement. For this reason, the company should consider implementing cross-selling campaigns by proposing complementary products or services that contribute less to overall revenue, as well as up-selling initiatives aimed at promoting premium versions of existing products. These actions may increase average order value while also encouraging more heterogenous purchasing behaviours and improving higher customer satisfaction.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
278 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 129 0 R
/E (Regarding resource allocation, the company should mainly focus its marketing efforts on high-value and low-value customers. Retaining high-value customers is essential because they generate a large share of revenue. On the other hand, selected low-value customers could be targeted with specific campaigns aimed at increasing their engagement and spending. Customers in the middle segments appear to show more stable behaviour and may not require the same level of investment. Moreover, customer acquisition efforts should focus on attracting individuals with characteristics similar to those of existing high-value customers. The results of the RFM and CLV analyses show that the most valuable customers are those who purchase frequently and remain actively engaged over time. Therefore, rather than focusing only on increasing the number of new customers, the company should prioritize attracting customers who are likely to purchase regularly and build a long-term relationship. Ultimately, these insights can support the marketing analytics team in informing managerial decisions on loyalty programs, customer retention, promotional strategies, resource allocation, and customer acquisition.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
